  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 11,
  "Question": "Which of the following describes the graph of the equation \\((x + y)^2 = x^2 + y^2?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "the empty set",
    "B": "one point",
    "C": "two lines",
    "D": "a circle",
    "E": "the entire plane"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Expand the squared sum to reveal which terms remain after cancellation:\n\\[\nx^2+2xy+y^2=x^2+y^2\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n2xy=0.\n\\]\nIf \\(x=0\\), any real \\(y\\) works. If \\(x\\ne0\\), dividing by the nonzero number \\(2x\\) gives \\(y=0\\). Conversely, every point with \\(x=0\\) or \\(y=0\\) satisfies the original equation.\n\nThe equation \\(x=0\\) describes the \\(y\\)-axis, and \\(y=0\\) describes the \\(x\\)-axis. The graph therefore consists of \\(\\boxed{\\text{two lines}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
